  "method": "Real decode loop plus exactly one extra invocation of one component per occurrence, output to scratch. Each probe arm is bracketed by baseline arms and measured against their mean, so a linear trend in time cancels; each probe is compared against its own local drift.",
  "claim_boundary": "Marginal in-loop costs, end-to-end on this GPU at capacity 70, so absolute figures are NOT comparable to n7b and only arm-to-arm differences are. Every marginal is a LOWER BOUND: the replicated call finds part of its data warm in L2, and extra work at the end of a layer gives the copy stream more room to hide. Marginals are not shares of the MoE term and do not sum to it. Nothing here is converted to tokens per second, and the part the marginals do not cover is reported as a number and not given a name."
